<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
    <h2>Clarity in the evidence and the next action.</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Business outcomes first</h3>
        <p>Define what matters to the business before choosing channel metrics. Distinguish attention and visits from qualified leads, customers, and revenue.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Evidence with context</h3>
        <p>Explain the source and limits of a finding. Treat assumptions as assumptions, and account for changes such as seasonality, budgets, or the customer mix.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Focused execution</h3>
        <p>Make priorities understandable and actionable. Connect each recommendation with the problem it addresses, an owner, and a way to review progress.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Learning over time</h3>
        <p>Use the results of each round of work to make the next decision. Sustainable growth needs a process that can adapt as customers and channels change.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

